.TH DELTOS 1 "September 2026" "deltos 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deltos \- turn photos of documents into flat, upright, correctly-sized scans
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deltos
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIIMAGE\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deltos
takes a photograph of a document at any angle and returns a flat, upright page
with its real physical dimensions, which it can export as PDF, PNG or JPG.
.PP
The page is located with a neural detector and classic edge detection together,
its true proportions are recovered from the perspective using the focal length
recorded by the camera, and its physical size comes from a reference card lying
beside it, the camera's depth measurement, or the standard paper size it
matches. It is then rectified, its lighting evened out, and turned upright.
.PP
Without \fB\-\-no\-gui\fR the images open in a window; with it the analysis is
printed and, with \fB\-\-out\fR, written to a file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gui
Run headless. Without it the images open in the window.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Write the result.
.I .pdf
takes any number of images, one page each;
.I .png
and
.I .jpg
take exactly one. Without it only the analysis is printed. Applies only
together with \fB\-\-no\-gui\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " MODE"
.IR color " (default), " gray " or " bw .
.TP
.BI \-\-strength " 0-100"
Enhancement strength, 50 by default. Its meaning depends on the mode: it blends
the enhancement in colour and grayscale, and sets the threshold in black and
white.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " FILE"
DocAligner ONNX model to use, instead of the one shipped with the program.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-model
Use edge detection alone.
.TP
.BI \-\-focal " PX"
Camera focal length in pixels. Taken from the EXIF metadata by default.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-focal
Estimate the focal length from the image rather than from EXIF.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-snap
Do not snap the aspect ratio to a standard paper size.
.TP
.B \-\-ocr
Also read the text of each page. It is printed here, and can be selected with
the mouse in the window.
.TP
.BI \-\-ocr\-lang " SPEC"
Tesseract language or languages for \fB\-\-ocr\fR, joined with
.RB ` + '.
The first one is the primary language. Defaults to the language last picked in
the window, otherwise to the system language paired with English.
.TP
.B \-\-bgr
Feed the model BGR instead of RGB.
.TP
.BI \-\-dpi " N"
Page density for images whose physical size is unknown. 300 by default.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DELTOS_DEBUG
Draws the detected quadrilateral on the source image and saves it under this
name. With several images, \fI\-1\fR, \fI\-2\fR and so on are inserted before
the extension.
.TP
.B DELTOS_ORIENT_DEBUG
Print the score of each rotation the orientation fallback tried.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/deltos.conf
The recognition language and whether the phone receiver is on.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/deltos/tessdata
Language models downloaded through the window, alongside those installed on the
system.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Analyse one photograph and print what was found:
.B deltos \-\-no\-gui photo.jpg
.TP
Turn several photographs into one PDF, each page at its own physical size:
.B deltos \-\-no\-gui \-\-out scan.pdf page1.jpg page2.jpg
.TP
Read a Greek page in black and white:
.B deltos \-\-no\-gui \-\-mode bw \-\-ocr \-\-ocr\-lang ell+eng bill.jpg
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tesseract (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Panayotis Katsaloulis
